        <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
          <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">In Dubai and across the UAE, photography can become a legal issue when it touches privacy or security. Taking photos of people without consent, especially women, families, accident victims, or beachgoers, can lead to serious penalties. Certain government and military sites are also off-limits, and even aircraft photography can be restricted. The UAE’s cybercrime law covers privacy violations involving photos, while official guidance clearly warns visitors to ask permission before taking pictures.</p>
        </mj-text>
